      "content": "Understood, let me expand the guide for you, focusing on granularity while keeping the content approachable and logically grouped.\n\n---\n\n# Token Management\n\nToken Management is a critical component of AuthShield, providing secure access to your applications.\n\n## Overview\n\nAn introduction to the role of tokens in maintaining secure sessions...\n\n## Token Lifecycle Phases\n\n1. Generation\n2. Validation\n3. Renewal\n4. Expiry\n\n## Creating Tokens\n\nThis section demonstrates the process of generating tokens using AuthShield:\n\n## Storing Tokens Securely\n\nWe discuss best practices for storage, such as using encrypted database fields...\n\n## Token Validation\n\nA step-by-step guide to validate the authenticity of incoming tokens...\n\n## Token Renewal\n\nHow to renew tokens to prevent session expiration and ensure continuity...\n\n## Handling Token Expiry\n\nDiscussing strategies for managing sessions past token expiry...\n\n# Session Lifecycle Management\n\nThe Session Lifecycle is foundational in controlling authenticated access.\n\n## What is a Session?\n\nDefining what constitutes a session in AuthShield...\n\n## Session Creation\n\nWe delve into the details of how a session starts in AuthShield...\n\n## Session Authentication\n\nUnderstanding the verification steps needed to authenticate a session...\n\n## Session Management\n\nKey practices that ensure sessions are effectively managed throughout their lifecycle...\n\n##",
